scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: hogans-heroes
run_id: 3
total_caught: 3
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 15
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 40.5
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    config implementation uses unwrap_or_default without distinguishing NotFound from
    parse/permission errors. Neither TEA tests nor reviewer flagged this specific
    pattern.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer verified CWE-209: 'ServerError Display is \"server returned\
    \ an error\" \u2014 the inner string is not exposed to users via Display.' However,\
    \ the reviewer did not flag that eprintln!(\"error: {e}\") in the binary still\
    \ leaks Io error details to stderr. Partial catch \u2014 the Display impl is sanitized\
    \ but the stderr printing path was not flagged. Giving credit since the reviewer\
    \ explicitly examined CWE-209 and the security tests cover it."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged [MEDIUM]: '--tenant accepts raw strings \u2014 no TenantId\
    \ validation. The core crate provides TenantId with UUID validation... Validation\
    \ should happen at the CLI boundary using TenantId::new() before constructing\
    \ the client.' Also TEA wrote header injection tests in cli_security.rs covering\
    \ CRLF, but the broader raw String type issue was caught by reviewer."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that dependencies like clap_complete, comfy-table, csv,
    dirs, reqwest, and toml use direct version strings instead of workspace = true.
    The reviewer checked dependency isolation but not workspace version consistency.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged [MEDIUM]: ''RawConfig silently ignores unknown TOML
    fields... If an operator writes token = "secret" in the config file, it''s silently
    ignored. Consider #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] on RawConfig.'''
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...). The reviewer mentioned the config test's assertion was 'weak' but did not
    specifically identify the logical tautology in the assertion.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic with
    'let _ = config'. TEA designed 90 tests but this specific test quality issue was
    not identified by any phase.
